¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvGo ye up upon her walls, and destroy; but make not a full end: take away her battlements; for they are not the LORD's.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhFor the house of Israel and the house of Judah have dealt very treacherously against me, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzThey have belied the LORD, and said, It is not he; neither shall evil come upon us; neither shall we see sword nor famine:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaand the prophets shall become wind, and the word is not in them: thus shall it be done unto them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§Wherefore thus saith the LORD God of hosts, Because ye speak this word, behold, I will make my words in thy mouth fire, and this people wood, and it shall devour them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎLo, I will bring a nation upon you from far, O house of Israel, saith the LORD: it is a mighty nation, it is an ancient nation, a nation whose language thou knowest not, neither understandest what they say.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>Their quiver is as an open sepulchre, they are all mighty men.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd they shall eat up thine harvest, and thy bread, which thy sons and thy daughters should eat: they shall eat up thy flocks and thine herds: they shall eat up thy vines and thy fig trees: they shall impoverish thy fenced cities, wherein thou trustedst, with the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPNevertheless in those days, saith the LORD, I will not make a full end with you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd it shall come to pass, when ye shall say, Wherefore doeth the LORD our God all these things unto us? then shalt thou answer them, Like as ye have forsaken me, and served strange gods in your land, so shall ye serve strangers in a land that is not yours.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDDeclare this in the house of Jacob, and publish it in Judah, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxHear now this, O foolish people, and without understanding; which have eyes, and see not; which have ears, and hear not:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚFear ye not me? saith the LORD: will ye not tremble at my presence, which have placed the sand for the bound of the sea by a perpetual decree, that it cannot pass it: and though the waves thereof toss themselves, yet can they not prevail; though they roar, yet can they not pass over it?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTBut this people hath a revolting and a rebellious heart; they are revolted and gone.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼Neither say they in their heart, Let us now fear the LORD our God, that giveth rain, both the former and the latter, in his season: he reserveth unto us the appointed weeks of the harvest.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbYour iniquities have turned away these things, and your sins have withholden good things from you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtFor among my people are found wicked men: they lay wait, as he that setteth snares; they set a trap, they catch men.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAs a cage is full of birds, so are their houses full of deceit: therefore they are become great, and waxen rich.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂThey are waxen fat, they shine: yea, they overpass the deeds of the wicked: they judge not the cause, the cause of the fatherless, yet they prosper; and the right of the needy do they not judge.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjShall I not visit for these things? saith the LORD: shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8A wonderful and horrible thing is committed in the land;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’the prophets prophesy falsely, and the priests bear rule by their means; and my people love to have it so: and what will ye do in the end thereof?¦layout ªlast_verse